# publish-check.patterns.example — template for operator-specific leak markers.
#
# Copy this to scripts/publish-check.patterns (which is gitignored) and replace
# the placeholders with YOUR private strings. publish-check.sh ORs every line
# below into its scan, on top of the generic built-in markers.
#
# Format: one POSIX extended-regex (ERE) per line. Blank lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Escape literal dots as \.
#
# Do NOT commit the real file — it exists to name the strings you never want
# pushed, so it necessarily contains them.

# Your hub/server hostnames (short names or FQDNs):
# myhost01
# hub\.internal\.example

# Your domains:
# example\.com

# Your operator usernames (as home-dir paths and as bare words):
# /home/(alice|bob)
# (^|[^a-zA-Z])(alice|bob)([^a-zA-Z]|$)

# Public/static IPs tied to your infrastructure:
# 203\.0\.113\.[0-9]

# Internal project codenames or private directories:
# \.myproject
